title: $:/plugins/bdawg/markdown-export-routes/readme
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

This plugin adds two HTTP routes to TiddlyWiki's integrated webserver for the $:/plugins/cdaven/markdown-export plugin, enabling programmatic Markdown export of tiddlers via REST API calls.

!! Single Tiddler Export

Export a single tiddler's content as Markdown via its title:

```
GET /markdown/export/{encoded-title}
```

```
GET http://localhost:8080/markdown/export/HelloThere
```

Returns `text/markdown`. Returns 404 if the tiddler is not found. Use URL encoding for titles with special characters (e.g., brackets).

!! Bulk Export via Filter

Export multiple tiddlers matching a TiddlyWiki filter expression:

```
GET /markdown/filter/{encoded-filter}
GET /markdown/filter?filter={encoded-filter}
```

The filter can be passed as the first path segment or as a `filter` query parameter (path takes precedence).

```bash
# Export all Concept-tagged tiddlers as Markdown
curl -g 'http://localhost:8080/markdown/filter/[tag[Concept]]' -o concepts.md

# Export matching tiddlers as a ZIP archive (each in its own .md file)
curl -g 'http://localhost:8080/markdown/filter/[tag[Topic]]?extension=.zip' -o topics.zip
```

```bash
# Export all Concept-tagged tiddlers as Markdown
xh get 'http://localhost:8080/markdown/filter/[tag[Concept]]' -o concepts.md

# Export matching tiddlers as a ZIP archive (each in its own .md file)
xh -d 'http://localhost:8080/markdown/filter/[tag[Topic]]' extension==.zip -o topics.zip
```

The ZIP option bundles multiple tiddlers into a valid binary ZIP archive, with each tiddler saved to its own Markdown file. Requires the tiddlywiki/jszip plugin.

!! Export Targets

From version 0.9 of the cdaven markdown-export plugin, you can choose between different "targets" that affect frontmatter, link formats, and other output specifics:

|Target|Description|h
|`pandoc` (default) |Pandoc-compatible Markdown with extensions |
|`obsidian` |Obsidian-flavoured Markdown |
|`logseq` |Logseq-flavoured Markdown |

Set the export target by editing the $:/plugins/cdaven/markdown-export/exporttarget system tiddler. The selected target applies to all routes.

!! Architecture

The plugin provides two route modules (both `module-type: route`, priority 100):

* `/markdown/export/(.+)` — single tiddler export, uses $:/plugins/cdaven/markdown-export/md-tiddler.js
* `/markdown/filter(/(.*))?` — filter-based bulk export, uses $:/plugins/cdaven/markdown-export/markdown-export.js

!! Source Code

The source code is available at https://github.com/berney/tw5-markdown-export-route/ -- this is where you can report issues or request features.
